{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793018588,"nonce":"oJ3Kl6AtTlJJP1RGiNqF7gKfIbA=","title":"Studio: bridge canvas selection and Presentation input","message":"Status: planned; implementation has not started.\n\nParent: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\nProgram epic: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\nCross-repository integration: RayDE:c299bb980e54d48d600312f31a178213d13bc56bc2d3967c4bf42ef9816d6671\nPhase: 2\n\nScope\nProvide coordinate-correct hit testing and selection overlays between CanvasKit content coordinates and real component/layout nodes. Support zoom/pan, transformed/clipped nodes, hierarchy selection, marquee and manipulation callbacks. Define exclusive input routing: Edit mode owns selection/manipulation; Presentation forwards component pointer, keyboard, focus, text/IME and scrolling in its preview context. Prevent the same event being processed by both modes.\n\nAcceptance\nSelection agrees with visible paint order at several zoom levels. Edit gestures do not activate component buttons or type into them. Presentation exercises real controls, scrolling, focus and composition; mode switches release capture and clear stale interaction state.\n\nDepends on\n- ashui:3a53c8c3514ad635f0e9dd49d38bb3103ae58b25015363b0030e756241b511ea — Studio: implement a reusable subtree renderer for CanvasKit\n- ashui:09749d70415c99561af5976b00ebbdd38844f6a9c1860e4bdaf1c728d046aa12 — Studio: expose versioned component and layout inspection data\n\nKeep implementation and validation evidence in this tracker. Follow the parent gate decisions; link any additional concrete runtime/backend prerequisite discovered by the feasibility work. No cloud deployment or new backend language is implied by this planning issue.","files":null}]}